a and in his mind that means her  being free of him  this could even possibly be mikasa and  aaron connecting through the paths  as aaron did before with the other  aldians i love to see them hugging  outside of that idyllic cottage house  they got going on  and it goes to show how many options we  have in life and how much different  our lives can be depending on the  decisions we make let me know your  thoughts  would it have been better if aaron had  chosen to go out like this  do you look at the 145th king's decision  to create  parody and await their deaths in peace  in a different light now  in many ways this cottage world would  have been an easier decision for aaron  to make  because he wouldn't have to undergo such  horrors himself but at the same time it  would have most likely meant  more horrors for parody island we then  jumped to aaron's colossal titan  punching armins in the face with his  hardened fists  you gotta love the hardened fists move  and if it even did damage on the armor  titan's face  you can bet it will do so on the less  defended colossal titan  reiner is being attacked as is peak and  annie  we'll see what happens here but if  things keep going like this  we may actually get jean connie and or  gabby turning back at the humans after  they consume one of these shifters  i'm hoping annie will survive and have  some sort of future with armin even if  it's short-lived and i can see gabby and  falco surviving together too  but reiner who's been fantasizing about  death may well die  unless isayama wants to keep trolling us  with the unbelievable luck of the plot  armored titan  it's ironic that this guy who keeps  wanting to die and keeps throwing  himself  in death's way keeps coming out of every  situation alive somehow so i honestly  wouldn't even be surprised if he makes  it out of this too  then we see mikasa refuse aaron's  request which although  it was delivered in that fantasy world  seems to convey aaron's true thoughts to  her in this world as well  she refuses to get rid of the scarf and  to forget about him  she actually tightens it around herself  and tells everyone else that she'll kill  aaron who's residing in the mouth of the  titan again  aaron might have communicated to her  that he's in the mouth  because he wants her to kill him so the  aliens will be thought of as the heroes  who stop the devil it's a team effort  and the core characters like armin and  levi  help mikasa get inside aaron's mouth now  that's a weird sentence  inside the mouth she sees aaron's head  there and smiles as she cuts it off  she says see you later aaron and we have  the two worlds overlapping here they  kiss in both the cottage world  and here where aaron's head has been  sliced off  and so we got the kiss we've been  begging for  for so long although definitely not in  the way we probably expected  and honestly something like this is  classic isayama you always have a darker  twist to the romance  but damn that was an impactful kiss i  had a really old video on youtube about  the top 10 most epic anime kisses of all  time  before i had to take it down due to  copyright reasons you know how youtube  works but this definitely would make it  into my revised list  i'm so glad we got this kiss because the  series has been tiptoeing around their  romantic feelings forever  so it's so nice to get something  conclusive here we're told to the boy  who sought freedom  goodbye so it is a goodbye kiss and even  emir is over here smiling and i'm sure  we'll have many of our questions  answered in the next and final  chapter like what's historia saying but  wow what a crazy climax this was to the  series  in the middle of all this horror we got  such a romantic moment  shakespeare would be proud you  definitely got some romeo and juliet  vibes here  since even romeo and juliet both kiss  the other when they were dead  or thought they were dead and sorry for  those romeo and juliet spoilers but back  to attack on titan  why is amir smiling does she love seeing  the good side of humanity  or does that smile have something to do  with the possibility that if the fouling  titan dies without the centipede in it  she may finally be free and does have to  roam in the other world for the rest of  eternity we'll find out but she wanted  freedom from her enslaved existence  she wanted something to change so if  she's smiling that might mean she's  gotten what she wished for this chapter  was also a really huge run for mikasa  where she proved once and for all that  she wasn't a slave who had to protect  aaron  at all costs and she did that by slicing  off his head  clearly that is the opposite of  protecting someone and ironically even  though she was willing to kill him she  refused to stop  loving him as he wanted her too talk  about your complicated love stories  by killing the one she loved she proved  that she loved him out of free will and  not  out of some brainwashed ackerman thing  can't wait to find out  more about everything in the next  chapter although you gotta expect that  isayama like many others  could well leave a lot of things  ambiguous and open to interpretation  nevertheless this is a great chapter  and probably the most romantic one  despite the tragic circumstances that is  it for this one and we only have one  more chapter to go  people let me know if you loved this one  or hated it and what you want from the  final  chapter ever i did my first attack a  time chapter review almost four years  ago now  and it's crazy to think how far the  story has come since then and how far  the channel has come since then too  thank you guys for being along for this  crazy amazing ride  and i hope you'll join me next month  when i cover  in probably a bittersweet way the final  chapter ever  of attack on titan it's tragic that our  protagonist seems to be gone for good  but i think we all predicted that would  be the outcome and having accepted that  i'm so glad we got that kis